39
00:03:10,033 --> 00:03:11,653
Let me try something.

40
00:03:11,653 --> 00:03:18,748
A new team member builds the image as node-api:main (no registry in the name) and pushes it:

41
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:24,596
The first line of the push output names the repository Docker used:

42
00:03:24,596 --> 00:03:26,731
docker.io/library/node-api.

43
00:03:26,731 --> 00:03:31,079
An image name without a registry host means Docker Hub,

44
00:03:31,079 --> 00:03:35,347
and library/ is reserved for Docker's official images,

45
00:03:35,347 --> 00:03:41,355
so the push is refused (or, with too many anonymous requests, rate-limited).

46
00:03:41,355 --> 00:03:44,992
The name decides the destination (lesson 077):

47
